'''MIRACLE SUMMER: Challenging the Pokémon Trading Card Game World Championships''' (Japanese: '''{{j|ミラクルサマー ～ポケモンカードゲーム世界大会への挑戦～}}''' ''MIRACLE SUMMER: Challenging the {{tt|Pokémon Card Game World Championships|Pokémon Trading Card Game World Championships}}'', Chinese: '''{{lang|zh-cmn-Hans-CN|逐梦之夏~向宝可梦卡牌世界大赛发起挑战~}}''' ''Summer of Chasing Dreams: Challenging the {{tt|Pokémon Card World Championships|Pokémon Trading Card Game World Championships}}'') is an hour-long live-action documentary that was released on [[YouTube]] in Japanese and on Bilibili in Chinese on December 6, 2024, and on YouTube with Japanese subtitles on December 29, 2024. It was announced with a trailer that was released on YouTube and X (formerly Twitter) in Japanese and on Bilibili, Weibo, Xiaohongshu, and Douyin in Chinese on November 29, 2024.

==Logos==
<gallery>
MIRACLE SUMMER Chinese logo.png|Chinese logo
</gallery>

==Plot==
{{incomplete plot}}
The documentary tells the story of Nii., a player of the Simplified Chinese version of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]], in reaching the [[2024 Pokémon World Championships]] in August 2024.

